# Build time configuration for the published extension.
#
# Committed on purpose. Everything here is a public URL that has to be baked
# into the artifact uploaded to the Chrome Web Store, and passing it on the
# command line instead meant a build that forgot it shipped with the Get help
# form silently hidden and no error anywhere.
#
# Do NOT put VITE_BACKEND_URL here. That is the address of a particular
# customer's backend, it differs per install, and baking one in would both leak
# that customer's hostname and pre-fill the wrong server for everyone else. It
# belongs in .env.development for local work, and nowhere else.

# Where the Get help form and the hosting waitlist post to. A fork that runs no
# support mailbox can empty this: the extension then hides both forms and points
# people at the issue tracker instead.
VITE_SUPPORT_URL=https://b24.palworks.ai
